  "aiContextParagraph": "The leadership at NVIDIA has undergone significant shifts in recent weeks following the initial resignation of Jensen Huang. Huang stepped down from his role as CEO amidst allegations involving espionage and personal misconduct. Following his departure, the company temporarily appointed Colette Kress to lead its operations while partners like Microsoft expressed ongoing confidence in the firm. However, the situation evolved when US President Donald Trump intervened, advocating for Huang to be given a second chance to lead the technology corporation. Following this public support, NVIDIA officially reappointed Huang as CEO. Most recently, President Trump indicated that he is open to providing a presidential pardon for Huang concerning the criminal allegations linked to his previous tenure, although he noted such action might not be strictly necessary at this stage.",
